Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Tier: Advanced
;
; Increase game scheduling priority and GPU priority.
; Tells Windows to give more CPU and GPU time to MMCSS-aware games.
;
; CARGO-CULT NOTE (CURSOR-AUDIT #12): NetworkThrottlingIndex=0xffffffff
; (line below) is a Windows 7/8-era multimedia myth. The setting was
; originally designed to throttle non-multimedia network packets when
; an MMCSS-tagged audio thread was active. By Win10 22H2 / Win11, MMCSS
; rarely throttles networking at all; flipping this to 0xffffffff
; produces negligible measurable latency change in modern gaming
; benchmarks. Left here because (a) it is harmless and (b) some users
; like to see "all knobs maxed" — kept opt-in via this individual .reg
; rather than added to apply-all.reg.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Multimedia\SystemProfile\Tasks\Games]
"GPU Priority"=dword:00000008
"Priority"=dword:00000006
"Scheduling Category"="High"
"SFIO Priority"="High"

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\Multimedia\SystemProfile]
"SystemResponsiveness"=dword:00000000
"NetworkThrottlingIndex"=dword:ffffffff
